Ratchet's supervisor uses a language model for diagnosis and structured function calling.
The Python backend collects metrics, sends them to the active model, executes requested tools,
and records the results for the dashboard.

Model providers

- For local inference, run the compiled llama-server with the model alias named in smartbackend/config.yaml.
  The default is llama3.2. Set LLAMA_CPP_BASE_URL if the server listens somewhere other than http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1.
- For cloud inference, configure the active provider in smartbackend/config.yaml and set its API key in the
  environment. The supervisor connects to the provider directly.

The supervisor runs every 60 seconds by default. Its Python tools collect metrics, read recent logs,
restart services, stop processes, clear caches, send alerts, and write local reports.
